 "captions": [
  {
   "id": "B1.c1",
   "beat": "B1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 12,
   "e": 18,
   "text": "Every 30 seconds of a night's sleep gets a label: Wake, N1, N2, N3 or REM. Experts score them by hand."
  },
  {
   "id": "B1.c2",
   "beat": "B1",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 18.7,
   "e": 23.2,
   "text": "Can a computer do it from one EEG channel, a single pair of scalp electrodes?"
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c1",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 28.9,
   "e": 37.3,
   "text": "A 2026 paper in Scientific Reports says yes: about 83% accuracy, combining a synchrosqueezed transform, a CNN, contrastive learning and a GRU."
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c2",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 38,
   "e": 42.1,
   "text": "We set out to reproduce it. Within our time and compute, we could not."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3.c1",
   "beat": "B3",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 51.8,
   "e": 59.1,
   "text": "So we changed the question. Not “how high can one number go?” but “does it still work on a person the model has never seen?”"
  },
  {
   "id": "B3.c2",
   "beat": "B3",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 59.8,
   "e": 62.9,
   "text": "And can we explain every step from first principles?"
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c1",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 67.1,
   "e": 75.3,
   "text": "Our data is Sleep-EDF, a public PhysioNet set: healthy adults recorded at home on cassette recorders, usually two nights of about 20 hours."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c2",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 76,
   "e": 82.6,
   "text": "Trained technicians then scored every 30-second epoch by hand, following the 1968 Rechtschaffen and Kales rules."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c3",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 83.3,
   "e": 90.2,
   "text": "We use 20 people and 39 nights: 42,307 epochs. Trimmed to its scored span, a night is about 1,085 epochs, or 9 hours."
  },
  {
   "id": "B4.c1",
   "beat": "B4",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 95.9,
   "e": 102.8,
   "text": "The paper chains four ideas. Ours is three plain ones: a short-time Fourier transform, a CNN and a bidirectional GRU."
  },
  {
   "id": "B4.c2",
   "beat": "B4",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 103.5,
   "e": 111.6,
   "text": "We dropped the contrastive stage: reproducing it failed within our time and compute, and we wanted a chain we can draw, derive and check."
  },
  {
   "id": "B4.c3",
   "beat": "B4",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 112.3,
   "e": 116.4,
   "text": "We make no claim that it helps or hurts: we never ran that comparison."
  },
  {
   "id": "B5.c1",
   "beat": "B5",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 122.1,
   "e": 129,
   "text": "The paper uses a synchrosqueezed transform. We use a plain STFT: a 2-second Hamming window sliding in 1-second steps."
  },
  {
   "id": "B5.c2",
   "beat": "B5",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 129.7,
   "e": 136,
   "text": "Each 30-second epoch becomes a 129 × 29 picture of frequency over time. A CNN squeezes it into 128 numbers."
  },
  {
   "id": "B5.c3",
   "beat": "B5",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 136.7,
   "e": 143.7,
   "text": "A bidirectional GRU then reads 20 neighbouring epochs forwards and backwards, because sleep is a story, not a snapshot."
  },
  {
   "id": "B6.c1",
   "beat": "B6",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 149.4,
   "e": 156.2,
   "text": "Testing is strict. Twenty people, ten folds: in each fold 16 people train, 2 choose the checkpoint and 2 are tested."
  },
  {
   "id": "B6.c2",
   "beat": "B6",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 156.9,
   "e": 162.7,
   "text": "Nobody appears twice. A person's epochs look alike, so splitting by epoch would flatter the score."
  },
  {
   "id": "B7.c1",
   "beat": "B7",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 169.4,
   "e": 176.2,
   "text": "First result: 56.42% macro-F1, a score that treats all five stages equally, averaged over people. Accuracy: 65.00%."
  },
  {
   "id": "B7.c2",
   "beat": "B7",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 176.9,
   "e": 183.6,
   "text": "Then we opened individual nights. On three of them the model was right on only 7.22%, 18.60% and 19.01% of epochs."
  },
  {
   "id": "B7b.c1",
   "beat": "B7b",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 187.8,
   "e": 194.2,
   "text": "Our hypothesis: nights differ in overall signal strength, so a model trained on some nights misreads others."
  },
  {
   "id": "B7b.c2",
   "beat": "B7b",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 194.9,
   "e": 200.5,
   "text": "A per-night yardstick cancels that, at a cost: a night's average also depends on its stage mix."
  },
  {
   "id": "B8.c1",
   "beat": "B8",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 204.2,
   "e": 211.1,
   "text": "Our idea, R1: judge every night against its own yardstick, using that night's own mean and spread for each frequency."
  },
  {
   "id": "B8.c2",
   "beat": "B8",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 211.8,
   "e": 217.6,
   "text": "Same architecture, retrained. Macro-F1 rose from 56.42% to 74.86%; accuracy from 65.00% to 80.99%."
  },
  {
   "id": "B8.c3",
   "beat": "B8",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 218.3,
   "e": 222.1,
   "text": "The three failing nights recovered to 82.54%, 88.68% and 84.87%."
  },
  {
   "id": "B9.c1",
   "beat": "B9",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 226.8,
   "e": 233.5,
   "text": "But R1 reads each test night's unlabeled signal within its scored span, and we chose it after the baseline failed."
  },
  {
   "id": "B9.c2",
   "beat": "B9",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 234.2,
   "e": 238.6,
   "text": "So it is offline and post-hoc: a promising finding, not a finished product."
  },
  {
   "id": "B9b.c1",
   "beat": "B9b",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 242.3,
   "e": 249.2,
   "text": "Our 80.99% sits near the paper's 83%. We do not rank them: the protocols differ, and R1 sees each test night's signal."
  },
  {
   "id": "B10.c1",
   "beat": "B10",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 255.4,
   "e": 260.2,
   "text": "A sensitivity check takes the statistics from the whole recording instead: 71.84%."
  },
  {
   "id": "B10.c2",
   "beat": "B10",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 260.9,
   "e": 268,
   "text": "Versus R1: −3.02 points, 95% interval −7.12 to +1.22. It crosses zero: no clear difference, but not proof they are equal."
  },
  {
   "id": "B11.c1",
   "beat": "B11",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 271.7,
   "e": 278.2,
   "text": "N1, the lightest sleep, stays hard: R1 recovers 44.69% of true N1 epochs, and 38.91% of its N1 calls are right."
  },
  {
   "id": "B11.c2",
   "beat": "B11",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 278.9,
   "e": 281.8,
   "text": "Three small attempts to fix it were all rejected."
  },
  {
   "id": "B13.c1",
   "beat": "B13",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 285.5,
   "e": 292,
   "text": "What we cannot yet say: that it works on new people. None of 78 audited participants is certified independent."
  },
  {
   "id": "B13.c2",
   "beat": "B13",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 292.7,
   "e": 295.6,
   "text": "Next: a locked protocol on truly independent data."
  }
 ]
}
